Z||000000||chris6878||10-31-1999||02:55 PM||||There are two metal  "pipes" coming out of the area where my trunk is behind my engine. both of which are cut off...  they may have went together...  was this a recall or something that was done??     <P>My car is an 85 se/gt.....  the vin # says its a 85, SE, 4ycl,     but if has the body of an 85 Gt or 86 SE (same)and has the V6 ..... so it could have possibly had a 4 cyl and was swapped for the v6 in it now...and someone just upgraded the body.  i dunno...       but my question is ... what are those two metal pipes comming from the trunk.. NOTE "you cant see the pipes from the inside of the trunk"||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||10-31-1999||03:03 PM||||If you will look in the rightside of your trunk, behind the carpet, you will see a blower motor.  This blower, pulls in cool air from the tire well and blow's it back into the engine compartment.  This is to assist in the cooling of the v-6 engine.  To my knowledge, only the v-6 cars, from 85-87, had this feature...but I may be wrong.<P>Brian||||reg||1
Z||000002||AL||10-31-1999||04:38 PM||||that motor only comes on when your car get's hot, or you turn on the air conditioner.||||reg||1
